    4. Assign stacking order TL(back), BR, BL, TR(front) and paint the output
    5. Derive input by placing each mask in its quadrant position within a 2Nx2M grid,
       coloring fg pixels with that quadrant's color, bg elsewhere
  notes: >
    Output-first guarantees valid overlap and stacking. Generate masks independently,
    then verify union coverage >= 80%; regenerate if too sparse.
